WEBVTT

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:19.830
Hello?

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.560
Ah, Onii-chan.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.480
It's me.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.000
Ikusu, stop making such absurd jokes.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.990
Oh, how did you know?

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.350
The incoming call number.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:31.840
Looks like this was a failure.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.770
Besides, the voice is completely wrong.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:37.680
Isn't that just a voice changer?

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.820
It doesn't have a natural sound because it's a machine.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:46.690
It seems like she uses a really efficient one, then.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.480
It also seems to be waterproof, and probably small.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.610
Once, she called from her bathtub.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.410
I see.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:59.230
So it's fine even when wet, and it's small enough to bring along...?

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:00.920
Okay, I understand!

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.700
I'll investigate along those lines.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.230
Look forward to the results.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:06.950
No, that doesn't-

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:07.940
Hey!

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.020
Miyabi!

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.020
Ah...

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.520
Good morning, Shougo-san.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.230
Oh, Konoe.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.440
What's wrong?

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.530
Ah, nothing.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:00.150
Come on, let's go.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.830
By the way, this is all about cars.

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:13.280
Speaking of cars, I bought a new car during the break.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.670
It's a cute car.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:15.960
Sensei!

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.300
What is it, Tanaka?

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.760
Instead of a car, wouldn't you want me to give you a piggyback ride instead?

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.140
Cut the crap!

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.930
I guess you wouldn't want one even if I tried to persuade you.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.140
Was that supposed to be something nice?!

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:31.640
I can feel your affection!

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.110
Kotori attack!

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.900
What happened between Kannagi-san and you?

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.390
What...?

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:42.070
Nothing.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:43.740
Please don't lie to me!

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.950
There was something strange about Kannagi-san today.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.580
It's like she changed back to the way she was before.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:55.250
When she was in her first year, she didn't make many friends,

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.590
and she always seemed lonely.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:03.950
She said I was secretly a pervert and that I had a big butt,

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:08.430
but I think she's better that way.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.640
So... So, um...

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:19.110
Konoe, I'm telling you this in confidence.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.440
Eh?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.700
So, I definitely want you to keep it a secret.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.450
A-All right.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.790
The truth is, Miyabi is...

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:48.800
As a joke, Mafu-sama hid a cuckoo bird.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:51.720
Here, the hidden cuckoo bird...

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:57.350
The meaning behind this is about siblings getting along well.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.980
What happened to Konoe?

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:04.740
All right.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.780
Konoe said she would help me when it was my turn to be on duty.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.740
Where on earth did she go?

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:16.960
Hello?

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:18.960
Um...

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.540
Hello? Hello?

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.280
Goodbye, Onii-sama.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.310
Hey!

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.190
Goodbye?

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:37.940
Why goodbye?

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.940
She's always calling out of the blue, and then suddenly...

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.570
A text from Ikusu?

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:48.950
What is this?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:52.740
Hello?

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.330
Hey, Shougo-kun.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:57.210
This time I used a restricted number.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.210
Stop being so misleading!

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:02.750
I may have discovered that voice changer.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:03.590
Eh?

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.300
IMT-270.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.720
I found it in the Kyoasu company's release schedule.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.850
It's a cell phone with that new feature built-in.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:14.220
That new feature...

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.090
That's right.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.730
It's a high-efficiency voice changer.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:21.600
There was a business venture that led to its engineering.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.990
It's a simple function, which has never been seen before,

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:27.610
and it allows you to make calls with the voice of performers and anime characters and such.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:31.120
However, immediately following its release, it was criticised.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.240
It was pointed out that it worked too well at changing voices,

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.830
and so it was feared it would be used to perpetrate a crime.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:39.670
So then...

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:41.330
It was recalled.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.710
It seems all the distributed phones were collected.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:49.840
By the way, the thing I sent you before was a picture of the phone.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:55.220
If there's somebody near you who has that mobile phone, then...

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:56.500
That can't be...

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.310
...that's probably who your mystery little sister is.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.270
Then... Then...

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.590
Hello?

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:07.230
Did something happen, Shougo-kun?

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.320
Shougo-kun?

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:09.950
So that's it?

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:10.820
That's how it was?

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.280
Yet... Yet I...

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.080
No running in the corridors!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.700
Please abide by the rules.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.320
Got it?

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:22.120
You already stand out enough, Mikadono-senpai.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:25.370
If you don't set a good example for the other students...

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:28.010
Kunitachi-san, President Tendou!

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.800
What is it?

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.130
I want to find Konoe.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.390
Tsuruma-senpai?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.390
Why?

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.060
I'll tell you the reason later.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:38.060
For now, just help me look for her.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.430
Even if you say that...

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.640
I understand!

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:42.730
President Tendou!

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.900
Mana, you search over there.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.280
Um... wait, President!

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:51.150
You can't run!

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.440
Ah, sorry.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:58.580
Mikadono.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.000
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.920
Could it be you became interested in Lyrical Sisters?

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.140
Senpai, excuse me.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.840
Hey, Mikadono!

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:09.710
Miyabi!

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:12.420
Wait!

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.930
Miyabi, I have a favour to ask.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:16.680
A favour?

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.310
Help me find Konoe.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.390
Why should I?

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:22.770
Please.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.870
Konoe, where are you?

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.370
<i>Goodbye, Onii-sama.</i>

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.750
Not here.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:52.300
Where?

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.800
Where are you, Konoe?

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:57.890
Where?

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.730
Ah! That's right!

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:09.650
Konoe!

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.320
Shougo-san.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:15.650
So you were here, as I thought.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.570
As you thought?

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:21.040
How did you know I was here?

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:22.450
That.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:29.170
When you called before, I heard the pigeons through the phone.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.880
So I thought you were probably here.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.760
Then, you already...

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.520
I'm sorry.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.020
I...

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:57.450
I'm Onii-sama's little sister.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:28.850
Do you remember the photo I sent with your birthday cake?

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:34.980
Yes, but I don't remember that very well because I
hurt my head around the time the photo was taken.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:39.990
That's a picture your father, Kumagorou-san, took and gave to me.

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:46.690
My father and yours were old friends, so because I was still small,

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:49.080
he took me with him to play with you.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.580
That's right... That day, too...

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:56.710
I was playing with Shougo-san and having lots of fun.

00:10:56.710 --> 00:11:00.340
Especially because the photo was taken on the day that I kissed you.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:03.140
Ever since then, I was always in high spirits.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:05.390
And then, on the way back...

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.680
Hurry, hurry!

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:10.480
Wait! Wait!

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.730
It's dangerous to run like that!

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:16.570
Hurry up!

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:22.870
Look out!

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.420
Shougo!

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:44.800
When I rushed over to you, do you know what you said?

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:48.750
You said,

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:52.810
"Look at me. I wonder if it looks like I protected you, like Gran Belion."

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.980
Gran Belion?

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.770
I wonder if I was trying to be a hero?

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:59.150
You didn't just try!

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:02.860
There is no doubt that you are my hero.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:05.620
This fact will never change.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.540
You're a hero and nobody could ever replace you!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:10.780
Konoe...

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:18.380
After that, my father and Kumagorou-san gradually stopped talking to each other,

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.550
so I wasn't able meet you anymore.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:24.410
So when I heard that you were transferring here,

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.140
I got really surprised.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.970
And what's more, on your birthday...

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.470
So, the present...

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:31.640
That's right.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:33.850
Even though I knew it was bad thing to do,

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:37.360
I had a look at the admission paperwork on top of Kotori-sensei's desk,

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:40.730
and found out the flat's address and your mobile phone number.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.240
I sent the cake, the photo of us together,

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.490
and the Gran Belion figure.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:51.160
I thought that once you've seen them, you might remember the things that happened back then.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:55.500
I understand that, but why did you have to use that phone?

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.500
Not only using the phone, but changing your voice as well.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:01.170
My father developed this phone.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:05.300
So that means, your father is Kyoasu's...

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.640
After he'd made a prototype, its sales were suspended.

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:12.390
He felt bad about it, so he finished making it in secret.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:14.430
Hm, Shougo-san...

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:16.190
Haven't you realised yet?

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:20.860
That voice is from a character in Gran Belion...

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:23.030
Ah, I see.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.990
That's the android, Perin-chan!

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.870
But Perin-chan was a maid, and not a little sister.

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:33.660
But she calls Gran Belion "Onii-sama"...

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:36.900
She only adored him like a brother,

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:38.170
but they were definitely not siblings.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:41.630
It looks like I was mistaken.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:45.550
My memories are fuzzy, as we were kids back then.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.500
So, does that mean...

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:51.470
To be honest, it was all a practical joke.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:58.600
You must have been surprised when you got the Gran Belion figure and the phone call from Perin-chan.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:13:59.940
Is that what it was?

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.690
But I thought my little sister was seriously trying to catch me.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:04.830
I'm sorry.

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:08.570
I never thought that things would get like this.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:12.530
I thought of stopping once,

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:15.500
but when I was talking to you with my identity hidden,

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.710
it felt like I had actually become your little sister.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.040
And that was quite fun!

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:23.670
So, what do you...

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:28.180
When we were kids, I always wanted to become your little sister.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:31.720
If that happened, I thought we could stay together forever.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:32.720
I see.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:37.520
But it looks like because of that, I've caused trouble for Kannagi-san.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:41.400
That was my misunderstanding, because I got the wrong impression.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:43.270
But I was the one who did it!

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:49.030
I even promised Kannagi-san that we'd stick to fair play when it came to dealing with you.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:53.160
And in the end, I'm sneaking around behind her back, like a cheat.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:55.700
<i>So you made a promise like that...</i>

00:14:56.950 --> 00:15:00.710
When you were being honest about
what had happened on the roof with me,

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:04.710
you told me things in confidence.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:08.130
Despite that, I was deceiving you.

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:09.630
It was difficult,

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.300
and I didn't know why you hadn't come to understand.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.180
So that's why you weren't in the classroom.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:20.100
When I saw you and Kannagi-san, my chest would tighten up.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:22.100
I wanted to go somewhere else.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:23.900
You were being silly.

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:27.110
If it's like that, you should have told me the truth earlier.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:27.570
But-

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:32.450
Konoe, you think of me as a hero, right?

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:35.330
So, in difficult times, or when you're in trouble,

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.660
let me help you out once more.

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.000
Shougo-san...

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:45.920
Ah!

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.800
W-What are you doing?!

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:52.360
You asked me to look for Tsuruma-san,

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:54.470
and then you ran off and left me.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:56.050
What's with this?!

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.270
Eh, no... This is...

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:00.100
Tsuruma-san as well!

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.640
You promised fair play, so why?

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.440
Um... That's not right.

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:06.900
There's a reason for this...

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.110
Then, what kind of reason do you have?

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:12.900
Would you mind telling me?

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:17.160
I see.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:21.080
So, Shougo was convinced that I was his little sister?

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:24.080
I'm sorry, it's my fault that...

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:26.670
No, it's my fault for jumping to the wrong conclusion.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:32.970
But now the misunderstanding has been resolved.

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:36.340
Now Shougo can marry me with no reservations.

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:37.970
Eh? Marry?

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:40.810
W-What is she talking about?

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:42.350
I have no idea what she's talking about.

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:46.330
Oh, so you forgot about that, like I thought.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:50.780
Shougo. When you were a kid, we had a pretend wedding.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:52.740
When I was a kid?

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.320
That's right.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.870
Shougo and I are childhood friends.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.530
Childhood...

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:00.080
...friends?

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.870
Eh?!

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:09.790
I was really surprised.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:13.380
Not just Konoe, but Miyabi was also friends with me back then...

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:18.030
When I explained to everyone who was helping look for Konoe,

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:20.140
they were surprised, as expected.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:24.140
But the one who was most surprised was me...

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.680
When I was hospitalised for hurting my head,

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:31.110
Miyabi's father was also there after getting injured.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:36.070
I was always clinging to my father, so I went with him to the hospital.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:38.530
I met you there while you were hospitalised.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:43.790
We played together in the courtyard until my father's medical examination was done.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:48.710
At first, I thought there was something strange about you.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:53.800
After all, you forgot a promise you made, just a short while after.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:58.260
Then suddenly, you would remember
the thing I thought you had forgotten.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:01.300
Around that time I was still having side-effects from the injury.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:04.600
A little while after I became friends with you...

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.270
One day, I realised...

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:09.150
...that I loved you!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:13.440
This was my first love.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:17.150
However, when my dad stopped going to the hospital,

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.240
I couldn't meet you anymore.

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.160
I cried everyday,

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:26.500
and prayed that I could meet you once more.

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:31.420
So when I heard that you were transferring here, I was really happy.

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:35.480
I thought that God must have heard my wishes from when I was a kid.

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.220
But, isn't it strange?

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:42.430
I didn't know what expression I should have when we actually met again.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:46.980
It seemed like you had totally forgotten about me.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:50.020
I wondered when you would remember about me.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:51.400
I'm sorry. I...

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:53.610
Honestly!

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:56.280
When you suddenly mentioned marriage,

00:18:56.280 --> 00:19:00.410
I thought for sure you had finally
remembered about our pretend wedding.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:02.050
I see.

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:04.530
That's why back then, you gave me an answer like that.

00:19:05.610 --> 00:19:07.790
<i>Who do you want to marry?</i>

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:10.620
<i>Isn't it obvious?</i>

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.590
<i>It's you.</i>

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:17.630
<i>It's always been you.</i>

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:21.380
I am serious about wanting to marry Shougo.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:24.430
If that's the case...

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:27.100
I'm also going to get married to Shougo-san!

00:19:27.510 --> 00:19:28.180
What?

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:30.270
Hey! Don't get in my way!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:31.850
S-Same to you!

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:33.690
What? Wanna fight?

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:34.480
Of course!

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:36.860
Hey, both of you-

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:40.450
All right. I accept your challenge.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:45.580
But, Tsuruma-san, this time round, you really have to use fair play!

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:47.580
Sure.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:48.830
Don't just go "sure"!

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.030
All right then, the contest starts tomorrow morning.

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:52.920
Is that okay?

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.210
Of course.

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:55.380
I won't lose!

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:57.840
Listen to other people!

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:07.850
In the end, the Ganizeus shampoo bottle bought from the hospital shop was just something she kept and treasured.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:10.850
Afterwards...

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.860
<i>I'm your little sister.</i>

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:17.340
Eh?

00:20:17.340 --> 00:20:19.650
On the day of Kumagorou-san's funeral service?

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:23.360
I couldn't come to the funeral service.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:27.780
After all, the entrance exam for Miryuuin Academy happened to be on that day.

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:31.960
I didn't know which day the funeral would be held on.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:37.250
My dad only knew Kumagorou-san from going to the hospital.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.750
It didn't seem like they knew each other that well.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:43.010
I might still have a little sister.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:47.180
However, neither Konoe nor Miyabi is my little sister.

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.720
In other words, I might still have a little sister,

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:55.940
but she could be living in an unrelated place that I'm not aware of.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.820
Mikadono Shougo's little sister...

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:09.530
Shougo-san, please wake up!

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:12.290
If you don't hurry up, you're going to be late!

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.290
W-Why?!

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.550
Y-Your outfit...

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:22.650
Shougo-san, when you were small,

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:25.640
you had a pretend wedding with Kannagi-san, right?

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:29.760
So, let's pretend to be newly-weds.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:31.180
If you don't do it, then it's not fair.

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:32.890
Not fair?!

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:33.940
Ah, Shougo!

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:34.980
You're finally awake.

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:37.580
Wha- Wha- Wha-

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:44.280
In the end, a man's romance is nudity.

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:45.630
That's right.

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:48.530
A newly-wed would wear nothing but an apron, right?

00:21:49.150 --> 00:21:50.270
It's a dream.

00:21:50.270 --> 00:21:51.740
It's a nightmare!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:55.210
This isn't a dream, Shougo-san.

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:56.960
That's right, Shougo.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:59.000
You have to face reality properly.

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:00.880
Right?

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:08.720
Ouch!

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:25.190
The love that ran away is searching for Eden

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:36.790
Despite losing my bearings, I understood the weight I felt from you

00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:42.420
We felt it on that summer day

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:48.510
Do you regret our meeting because of these painful lies?

00:22:48.510 --> 00:22:54.510
Are you saying it was only painful?

00:22:54.510 --> 00:23:02.150
Sweep away the coming tomorrow with those gentle hands

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:08.240
A promise forever from bygone days

00:23:09.110 --> 00:23:14.990
We will certainly be together, because I still believe in you

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:21.000
My pounding heart won't stop now

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:27.090
It has finally begun, that lovely thing

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:38.810
To a dazzling world of bewilderment with my heavenly lover

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:45.570
Shougo-san, have you forgotten the time when you kissed me when we were small?

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:47.400
Sorry, my memory isn't clear.

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:51.610
So Shougo, does that mean you've also forgotten about the time when we played doctors?

00:23:51.610 --> 00:23:53.660
Sorry, my memory isn't clear- Hey!

00:23:53.660 --> 00:23:55.580
As if something like that would happen!

00:23:55.580 --> 00:23:59.120
Have you forgotten about the time when we practised making babies?

00:23:59.120 --> 00:24:01.500
Hey guys! Give me a break!

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:04.540
Next time, Episode 5: Can't my little sister let me sleep?

00:24:04.540 --> 00:24:06.880
Everyone, don't forget to watch!

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:09.130
You promised me!
